---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const updated = '31 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy — StratumCore"
  description="How StratumCore Pty Ltd collects, uses, shares and protects personal information across our website, events, marketing and client engagements."
  canonical="https://www.stratumcore.com.au/privacy"
>
  <Nav />

  <main class="privacy">
    <div class="wrap">

      <header class="ph">
        <p class="page-label">Legal</p>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <span class="teal-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <p class="meta">
          StratumCore Pty Ltd &middot; ABN 61&nbsp;696&nbsp;477&nbsp;406<br />
          Last updated {updated}
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <p class="lead">
          This policy explains what personal information we collect, why we collect it,
          who we share it with, and how you can access or correct it. It applies to our
          website, our events, our marketing, and our client engagements.
        </p>
        <p>
          We are a small advisory firm. We do not sell personal information, we do not
          run advertising networks, and we do not trade in data.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are and how to contact us</h2>
        <p>
          StratumCore Pty Ltd is a Brisbane-based finance and cost advisory practice
          serving mining operators and asset-intensive businesses.
        </p>
        <p>
          Privacy enquiries: Wen Khong,
          <a href="mailto:wen@stratumcore.com.au">wen@stratumcore.com.au</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Contact and enquiry information.</strong> Your name, email address,
          phone number, job title and organisation, when you give them to us through our
          website, at an event, by email, or in the course of an engagement.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Event information.</strong> If you attend one of our events, including
          The Commercial Edge series, we collect your RSVP details, dietary requirements
          where you provide them, and a record of your attendance.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Engagement information.</strong> When we work with a client
          organisation, we handle information about that organisation&rsquo;s staff,
          contractors and suppliers as part of the work. This is covered in more detail
          under &ldquo;Client information&rdquo; below.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Business contact information from public sources.</strong> We identify
          potential clients and referral partners using publicly available sources such
          as company websites, professional networking sites, business registers and
          industry directories. The information we collect this way is business contact
          information: name, role, organisation and business contact details. If you
          would prefer we did not hold your details, tell us and we will delete them.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Website information.</strong> Our website collects standard technical
          information including IP address, browser type, pages visited and referral
          source. We use this to understand how the site is used. Where we run a
          campaign, we may record which link or QR code brought you to a page.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not collect sensitive information as defined in the Privacy Act, and we
          ask that you do not send it to us.
        </p>

        <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>To send you material you have asked for, such as a case study, template or toolkit.</li>
          <li>To respond to your enquiry and arrange meetings.</li>
          <li>To run our events and follow up with people who attended.</li>
          <li>To deliver our services under an engagement.</li>
          <li>To tell you about our services and events where you have consented or would reasonably expect it, and always with a way to opt out.</li>
          <li>To meet our legal, professional and record-keeping obligations.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Marketing and how to stop it</h2>
        <p>
          If you give us your email to receive a document, we send you that document and
          nothing else automatically.
        </p>
        <p>
          Any further contact from us is a person writing to you individually. You can
          stop it at any time by replying and saying so, or by using the unsubscribe link
          in any email. We will action it promptly and we will not ask you to justify it.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Our people.</strong> Our partners and subcontractors, who are bound by
          confidentiality obligations.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Event co-hosts.</strong> Our events are co-hosted with other firms. If
          you RSVP to a co-hosted event, your RSVP details are shared between the host
          firms so we can run the event and follow up. We tell you who the co-host is in
          the invitation.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Service providers.</strong> We use third-party services to run our
          email, calendar, website, file storage and mailing list. These providers hold
          information on our behalf and are not permitted to use it for their own purposes.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Where required by law</strong>, or where you have consented.
        </p>
        <p>
          We do not disclose your information to anyone else without your consent.
        </p>

        <h2>Overseas storage</h2>
        <p>
          Some of our service providers store information outside Australia, including in
          the United States and the European Union. By providing your information you
          consent to it being handled by those providers on our behalf. We take
          reasonable steps to use providers with appropriate security and privacy
          practices.
        </p>

        <h2>Client information</h2>
        <p>
          Information we obtain in the course of a client engagement is confidential. We
          treat it under the confidentiality obligations in our engagement terms and, as
          chartered accountants, under APES 110 <em>Code of Ethics for Professional
          Accountants</em>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Where we publish material about our work, such as a case study, we anonymise the
          client and generalise figures and details, and we do not publish anything
          identifying a client without their agreement.
        </p>

        <h2>Security and how long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          We hold information in access-controlled cloud services with multi-factor
          authentication. No system is completely secure, but we take reasonable steps to
          protect information from misuse, loss and unauthorised access.
        </p>
        <p>
          We keep marketing and event contact information until you ask us to remove it or
          until it is no longer useful. We keep engagement records for at least seven
          years to meet professional and tax record-keeping obligations, and then destroy
          or de-identify them.
        </p>
        <p>
          If a data breach occurs that is likely to cause serious harm, we will notify
          affected individuals and, where required, the Office of the Australian
          Information Commissioner.
        </p>

        <h2>Accessing and correcting your information</h2>
        <p>
          You can ask us what we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete
          it. Email <a href="mailto:wen@stratumcore.com.au">wen@stratumcore.com.au</a>. We
          will respond within 30 days. There is no charge.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Our website uses cookies for basic functionality and to measure how the site is
          used. You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, though some
          parts of the site may not work as well.
        </p>

        <h2>Complaints</h2>
        <p>
          If you think we have mishandled your information, email
          <a href="mailto:wen@stratumcore.com.au">wen@stratumcore.com.au</a> and we will
          respond within 30 days.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you are not satisfied with our response, you can complain to the Office of the
          Australian Information Commissioner at
          <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">oaic.gov.au</a>,
          by phone on <a href="tel:1300363992">1300&nbsp;363&nbsp;992</a>, or by post to
          GPO Box 5218, Sydney NSW 2001.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We update this policy from time to time. The current version is always on this
          page with the date it was last updated.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    background-color: var(--bg);
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-height) + clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 4.5rem));
    padding-bottom: var(--section-y);
  }
  .wrap {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-inline: var(--s-5);
  }

  /* ── Page header ── */
  .ph h1 {
    color: var(--head-on-light);
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 6vw, 3.25rem);
    margin: var(--s-3) 0 0;
  }
  .ph .teal-rule { margin: var(--s-5) 0; }
  .ph .meta {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  /* ── Prose ── */
  .prose > * + * { margin-top: var(--s-4); }
  .prose p,
  .prose li {
    color: var(--body);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: var(--lh-body);
    max-width: none;
  }
  .prose .lead {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 1.1875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    color: var(--head-on-light);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3.2vw, 1.65rem);
    margin-top: var(--s-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--s-4);
  }
  .prose strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .prose em { font-style: italic; }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    transition: color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease);
  }
  .prose a:hover { color: var(--accent-strong); }
  .prose a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  /* Bulleted list with a small accent dot, no default markers */
  .prose ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-2);
  }
  .prose li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.35rem;
  }
  .prose li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.62em;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
